messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C02
Scenario title: Afternoon Pickup and Caregiver Handover
Initial workflow description:
I arrange who will pick up my child and check that they got home. Sometimes the person collecting them changes during the day.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "Who are the people who may collect your child, and does the childcare provider hold a pre-approved list of authorised collectors that you maintain?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "When the pickup person changes during the day, what is the minimum that must happen for the change to be accepted — for example, is a phone call to the provider enough, or is written confirmation required?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Which channel or tool do you currently use to notify the childcare provider and the collector about pickup arrangements or last-minute changes?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "How do you confirm that your child has arrived home safely after pickup — what does that confirmation look like and who sends it?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What do you do if the expected collector has not arrived by a certain time and you cannot reach them — who takes over and what steps are followed?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "On a typical week, how many days does the pickup arrangement stay the same versus change, and do changes tend to happen at a particular time of day?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Afternoon Pickup and Caregiver Handover with explicit responsibilities, decisions and recorded completion.",
  "actors": [
    "mother",
    "partner",
    "backup caregiver",
    "childcare teacher"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "shared family calendar",
    "authorized pickup list",
    "childcare messaging app",
    "family handover log"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "pickup window",
    "collector availability",
    "authorized pickup names",
    "change request"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "confirmed collector",
    "provider acknowledgment",
    "collection confirmation",
    "home arrival note"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Review the pickup window",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Ask the planned collector to confirm availability",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check the collector against authorized pickup names",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Request a collector change from the teacher if needed",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Wait for provider acknowledgment before the changed pickup",
      "actor": "backup caregiver"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Collect the child and confirm collection",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Record home arrival in the handover log",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Follow up on a missing collection confirmation",
      "actor": "mother"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Is the proposed collector already authorized?",
      "branches": [
        "use the existing entry",
        "obtain provider acknowledgment before collection"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Has collection been confirmed by the end of the pickup window?",
      "branches": [
        "record completion",
        "contact the collector and the teacher"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "collector unavailable",
    "collector not authorized",
    "provider acknowledgment missing",
    "collection confirmation missing"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A1",
      "rationale": "Summarize pickup plans from the household calendar."
    },
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Send availability requests to the planned collector."
    },
    {
      "target": "A8",
      "rationale": "Remind the mother when a confirmation has not been logged."
    }
  ],
  "operating_context": {
    "frequency": "each scheduled childcare afternoon",
    "manual_effort": "The mother spends about five minutes confirming pickup when the original plan holds.",
    "data_availability": "The household can read its calendar and handover log, but only the provider updates the pickup list.",
    "integration_and_approval_constraints": "A new collector is not automatically approved; the teacher follows the fictional provider's agreed acknowledgment process."
  },
  "interpretation": "Activity dependencies describe the nominal sequence. Decision branches and exception descriptions qualify that sequence; this is not an executable BPMN model."
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
